    "about": {
        "captions": {
            "Library-Akkadian-Merchant": "When Ashur-Muttabbil died, things were bad. With no food and no money, with her husband's family against her, <a href=\"https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/326712\" target=\"_blank\">Kunanniya</a> didn&#39;t think that she would survive. “I'm going to die”, she wrote to her sister. But then an opportunity arose. A small one, a single bolt of cloth to be traded. Then another, then another. She took each one.</p> <p>Today, it is not her husband that leads caravans from Kanesh to Assur, it is her sons. One of her daughters supervises the weavers and artisans. The other is a high priestess of Anna. Kunnaniya herself presides over her records: the contracts, the trades, the accounts, the letters... and that final, precious message from Ashur-Muttabil: “Cheer up your heart”.</p>",
            "Library-Aksum-Man": "",
            "Library-Aksum-Woman": "",
            "Library-Alexandria": "",
            "Library-Angkor-Wat": "",
            "Library-Celtic-Comic": "",
            "Library-Contemporary-Amhara": "",
            "Library-Death": "",
            "Library-Dragon": "<p>Raouwa Da Horouwe Ra Mha (“The bright-eyed one who is as light as a daisy”) used to have a hoard of gold like any other self-respecting dragon. But lying on a pile of gold, waiting for the next metal-clad nitwit to come challenging quickly got boring. So she started buying books: first one, then two, then as much as the eager merchants could drag up her mountain.</p><p>Now the gold is gone, but she doesn&#39;t mind. In fact, she considers this her best decision since the time she decided not to eat that frightened girl the bishop offered, but snacked instead on the fat bishop and his men-at-arms. To be fair, her archival skills leave something to be desired. She once spent a month looking for a book and finally found it inside a well-chewed helmet of a long-forgotten knight.</p>",
            "Library-Gondar": "",
            "Library-Hermit": "",
            "Library-Inca": "",
            "Library-Khumbu": "",
            "Library-Lego": "",
            "Library-Maori-Pa": "",
            "Library-Maya-Tikal-Illustration": "",
            "Library-Maya-Tikal": "",
            "Library-Medieval-Europe-Illumination": "",
